  "summary": "Four candidate documents directly apply contrastive learning (representation learning with paired positive and negative examples) to crop/agricultural yield estimation. [V0048] (Brennan et al., 2018) evaluates on ToxiBench and reports F1=0.83. [V0045] (Gupta et al., 2024) evaluates on AgriSat-4 and reports accuracy=0.62. [V0046] (Haddad et al., 2025) evaluates on LedgerGuard and reports MAE=0.69. [V0047] (Adebayo et al., 2026) evaluates on CellLife and reports AUROC=0.76. A fifth document, [V0034], addresses agricultural yield but uses decentralised training without pooled records rather than contrastive learning, making it the closest non-contrastive agricultural yield study to round out five candidates. Documents that only mention contrastive learning for agricultural yield as prior work (e.g., [V0015], [V0066], [V0158], [V0217]) are excluded as they do not directly apply the method.",
